            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis seems to happen because 'mini.completion' tries to show signature information and fails due to an upstream error.\r\n\r\nI don't have any LSP server for Ada files installed (and would like to keep it that way if possible), so would you mind getting some debug information to help solve this issue?\r\n\r\nHere are the steps:\r\n- Execute the following (very long, but acceptable) command `:lua _G.log, orig = {}, vim.lsp.util.stylize_markdown; vim.lsp.util.stylize_markdown = function(...) table.insert(_G.log, {...}); return orig(...) end` .  This will wrap offending core function to track how it was called.\r\n- Reproduce the issue (preferably so that no information or signature help windows is shown prior to it).\r\n- Execute the following command `:lua vim.fn.append(0, vim.split(vim.inspect(_G.log), '\\n'))`. This will put some new lines at the top of the current buffer.\r\n- Copy new lines and paste them here.",
